 "notes": "The first rerun, by fallback 2 of slice 05, which was written before any data existed. E01 failed P1 at the published weight: sweet 3 gave MN9 7 to 22 spikes in ten seeds against the 32 asked for. The weight was then recalibrated on pilot seeds 0 to 2 only, by a rule written into the slice before the calibration ran: of 0.30, 0.35, 0.40, 0.45, 0.50, 0.60 and 0.70 mV, take the weight whose mean MN9 count at sweet 3 is closest to 80% of its mean count at sweet 4. The ratios were 0.26, 0.85, 0.19, 0.12, 0.04, 0.01 and 0.51, so the weight is 0.35 mV, and the sweep is 0.7, 1 and 1.3 times it. Every criterion is unchanged from E01. Fresh seeds: 200 to 209 confirm, 210 to 219 held out. Seen before this file was committed, and not used to change any criterion: at 0.35 mV the three pilot seeds gave sweet 3 counts of 111, 18 and 60, and above 0.40 mV a stronger weight made sweet 3 drive MN9 less, not more. The same early stop as E01. Controls, off the shipped model: 30 shuffled brains and three seeds per random population, as in E01.",
